Subject: [PATCH 116/116] Drive LPF: 2x oversampled where 1.2.1 did (high up
 with resonance), with v18's half-band filters

v18 ran the drive ladder 2x oversampled at every cutoff and resonance until the CPU was at its limit (cpuDireness
14). A song with many drive filters then needed 3.5 times real time at a bar's start (1.2.1: 1.7) and lost nearly all
its voices before the guard could act (tests/stress/audio, all LPFs on drive). It now oversamples where 1.2.1 did:
the cutoff above logFreq 51 << 24 with the resonance above 1.2.1's table there (from about 5 kHz at resonance 25,
13 kHz at 20, never below 15), where the resonance and the saturation alias audibly; lower down the ladder takes the
aliases away itself. Where it oversamples it does so as v18 (real half-band filters, images -88 dB). Switching stays
crossfaded; a quarter of an octave and a tenth of the threshold of hysteresis keep a cutoff or resonance moving
around it from switching back and forth.

tests/filters drive: where (0 of 10,251 settings differ from 1.2.1's condition; a sweep across the threshold and back
switches twice, a wobble around it once), alias at resonance 30 % (2x 3.7 to 21 dB better), toggle at cutoff 45. Below
the threshold the ladder sings as in 1.2.1: -56 cents at 2 kHz (v18 -30; the limit is now 60 cents there).

